# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# A section line through a stair draws what its plane cuts of the stair.
#
# A straight flight of 17 risers, 1 m wide, from (0, 0) to (3.6, 0), and a
# section along its walking line (y 0) looking to its left. The plane
# passes through every tread; the tread's faces toward the viewer lie
# before the plane, so its edges alone draw nothing of it. The plane's
# outline of each tread does (`append bim plane outline of`): the first
# tread's top at one riser's height, the sixteenth and last one's a riser
# under the storey's height. In the drawing x is the model's x + 1.
import ui/shell/bim_app_parts.dl

function check stair cut {boolean:passed} named {a string:label}:
    execute:
        if passed = false:
            print ((the string form of "FAIL: ") + label) as a line
        else:
            print ((the string form of "PASS: ") + label) as a line

# How much of the level stretch at `lineHeight` from `fromX` to `toX` the
# edges lying on it cover together, in millimetres (the plane's outline
# comes a line for each triangle it cuts, end to end).
function the stair cut cover of {a pointer to a list:edges} at {a 64 bit floating-point number:lineHeight} from {a 64 bit floating-point number:fromX} to {a 64 bit floating-point number:toX}:
    execute:
        set longest to 0.0
        loop cursor from 0 to the length of edges:
            set edge to the item at cursor in edges
            if ((the absolute value of (edge's start's y - lineHeight)) < 0.0001) and ((the absolute value of (edge's finish's y - lineHeight)) < 0.0001):
                set lowX to the maximum of fromX and (the minimum of edge's start's x and edge's finish's x)
                set highX to the minimum of toX and (the maximum of edge's start's x and edge's finish's x)
                if highX > lowX:
                    set longest to longest + (highX - lowX)
        return (the rounded value of (longest * 1000.0)) as an integer

set editor to a new bim editor
set target to the address of (editor's documentValue's current)
set stairId to add bim stair on editor's levelId from (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 3.6 and y 0.0) wide 1.0 in 17 risers of (the string form of "timber") to target
set sectionId to add bim section view from (a cad vector2 with x -1.0 and y 0.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 5.0 and y 0.0) to target
refresh bim editor (the address of editor)
set sceneList to the bim sketch meshes of editor's documentValue's current
set sectionView to the item at (the bim view index of sectionId in editor's documentValue's current)'s position in (editor's documentValue's current's views's values)
set sectionCut to the bim section of (editor's evaluation) from (sectionView's lineStart) to (sectionView's lineFinish)
set sectionEdges to the bim section projection of editor among (sceneList's values) for sectionView cut as sectionCut
set edges to sectionEdges's values
set stairValue to the item at 0 in (editor's documentValue's current's stairs's values)
set riserHeight to the bim riser height of stair stairValue in editor's documentValue's current
set stairEdges to 0
loop cursor from 0 to the length of edges:
    if (the item at cursor in edges)'s elementId = stairId:
        set stairEdges to stairEdges + 1
print ((the string form of "stair edges: ") + (the string form of stairEdges)) as a line
print ((the string form of "first tread's top (mm): ") + (the string form of (the stair cut cover of edges at riserHeight from 1.05 to 1.2))) as a line
print ((the string form of "last tread's top (mm): ") + (the string form of (the stair cut cover of edges at (riserHeight * 16.0) from 4.4 to 4.55))) as a line
check stair cut (stairEdges >= 68) named (the string form of "every tread the plane cuts draws its outline")
check stair cut ((the stair cut cover of edges at riserHeight from 1.05 to 1.2) = 150) named (the string form of "the first tread's top at one riser's height")
check stair cut ((the stair cut cover of edges at (riserHeight * 16.0) from 4.4 to 4.55) = 150) named (the string form of "the last tread's top one riser under the storey's height")
